### FILE PATH: C:/Users/ashay/Downloads/Quiz/QR-Code-Generator\script.js

**Error:**
1.  **Syntax Error:** `asynchronous` is not a valid keyword. It should be `async`.
2.  **Logic/Runtime Error:** `fetch` is an asynchronous operation but was called without `await`.
3.  **Missing Error Handling:** The API call was not wrapped in a `try...catch` block as per requirements.
4.  **Encoding Issue:** The input value is appended directly to the URL without `encodeURIComponent`, which will break if the user enters characters like `&` or `#`.
5.  **UI Feedback:** The "Loading..." text is never hidden if the logic fails or completes unless manually set.

**Fixed code:**
```javascript
const btn = document.querySelector('button');
const imgbox = document.getElementById('imgBox');
const qrImage = document.getElementById('Qr-Image');
const input = document.getElementById('Qr-text');
const loadelement = document.createElement('p');
imgbox.append(loadelement);

const getQR = async () => {
    loadelement.hidden = false;

    if (input.value.trim().length > 0) {
        qrImage.src = '';
        loadelement.classList.remove('invalid-input');
        loadelement.innerHTML = 'Loading ...';

        try {
            // URL encode the input to handle special characters correctly
            const apiUrl = `https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=150x150&data=${encodeURIComponent(input.value)}`;

            const response = await fetch(apiUrl);

            if (!response.ok) {
                throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
            }

            // For this specific API, the URL itself is the source for the image
            qrImage.src = response.url;
            loadelement.hidden = true;
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Error fetching QR code:', error);
            loadelement.innerHTML = 'Error fetching QR Code. Try again.';
            loadelement.classList.add('invalid-input');
        }
    } else {
        qrImage.src = '';
        loadelement.classList.add('invalid-input');
        loadelement.innerHTML = 'Invalid Input !';
        loadelement.hidden = false;
    }
}

btn.addEventListener('click', getQR);
```

